{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990213-how-are-masques-reflected-in-the-astral","id":990213,"title":"How are Masques reflected in the Astral?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-19T19:27:57-07:00","id":990213,"title":"How are Masques reflected in the Astral?","content":"I'm playing a Mind-focused Guardian that is going to be heavily invested in both Astral-related phenomena and Masques. Which got me thinking: do you think Masques have a reflection in a mage's Oneiros? If so, do you think it'd be a &quot;place&quot; in the Astral, or maybe a denizen, or even a fully realized goetic being? If they aren't naturally goetia, do you think a mage could solidify it into one, and if so what level of Mind do you think that would fall under? My gut says 4 because of Patterning but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Curious to hear your thoughts on this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:53:05-07:00","id":990438,"title":"","content":"Astral Realms describes the Oneiros as being divided into individual &quot;cells&quot; that reflect specific memories, hopes, fantasies, fears, etc. Specific game traits like Vice have their own large realm, and in 2E I imagine there are cells for each Aspiration and Obsession.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that each Masque is a sub-realm of the Oneiros with its own sparsely populated cells for the Masque's Virtue and Vice and imagined memories. Maybe when the mage is adopting a certain Masque, their Daimon changes to fit said Masque and encourage the mage to live up to it. Playing out imagined memories and dreams and other moments in the Masque-Oneiros could be a good excuse to raise that Merit by strengthening the identity. Imagine playing a kind of association game where you create new cells on the fly (with a Patterning Mind spell maybe?) by following scenes to their natural conclusion and seeing where they lead in this constructed mind. And imagine how unsettling it will be when your strengthened Masque starts generating new cells on its own.*<br /> <br /> <i>*talk to your Epopt before gardening your own Oneiros for magical power. side effects may include headaches, dissociation, and (legion).</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-20-2016, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:55:42-07:00","id":990441,"title":"","content":"I'd do it thus, YMMV:<br /> <br /> There is a chamber in the Oneiros that represents one's face. In many people, this is <i>also</i> the throne room of the Ego, that represents will. The two concepts <i>should</i> be directly connected...<br /> <br /> Masques would sit in the same array as any other fronts you put up, just more mystically significant than the rest. As such, yes, there really must be an astral representation.<br /> <br /> One guy might literally have a chamber of faces, (like the witch in that one Oz book) while another might simply have a set of carved masks. An old school slide projector with slides and a screen could work, too. A gallery of paintings is a bit farther afield, but it could work for some takes, especially if there is a mirror and makeup kit in the gallery. <br /> <br /> Some astral thing would select which face is being worn. (the faceless thing or a bust, for the faces approach. The slide projector itself, for that one.)<br /> <br /> If the Masque is a ranked Goetic, this selector needn't be. If this selector is, the Masque needn't be. Either <i>could</i> be. <i>Both</i> could be, too. <br /> <br /> I'd make the choice on preference for themes to emphasize. If Masques are tapping a universal Truth, as the Guardians believe, then the symbols in the Astral might remain passive objects that literally transform the wearer like a spell. (e.g. A wooden mask that, when worn, turns you into the creature represented.) If Masques represent a Guardian creating an identity from his own mind, they should probably be animate identities inside the Oneiros with their own personalities (albeit thin) with some mystical tell.<br /> <br /> That said, if you are not in the chamber of faces, it should be possible that you run into every major face you have, Masques especially so. The trick is, if they are their own personalities or transform another, you really wouldn't easily be able to distinguish. Your Daimon wearing the masque would behave differently than your Vice, though.<br /> <br /> Much as petty temptations wander around with limited personality, an empty Masque could, as well, I suppose. If it acts more complex, it's probably being worn, then, I suppose.<br /> <br /> <br /> You could select the particulars based on the mage in question, making the different choices <i>really</i> subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}